144	// Real install/remove — per-source adapters over SSH.
145	//
146	// Approach: the worker resolves a DIRECT download URL from the source's API, then
147	// SSHes into the game VM and has the VM itself `curl` the file into the game's
148	// plugin/mod directory (deterministic filename, so uninstall is a plain rm — no
149	// per-install state to track). Sources that need auth or per-repo handling
150	// (GitHub release zips, Nexus, CurseForge key, Codefling paid) soft-fail with a
151	// clear "install manually from <url>" note rather than faking success.
152	//
153	// Supported today: modrinth + spigotmc (Minecraft), umod (Rust), thunderstore
154	// (Valheim) — which fully covers those three games' catalogs.
155	// ===========================================================================
